cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this index, cite the dated release you used; the list is at https://leadgreen.ai/api/v1/releases/index.json."
type: dataset
title: "Green Tokens: GPU energy per million output tokens, by model, GPU and configuration, with grid carbon intensity"
version: "2026-10-19"
date-released: "2026-10-19"
url: "https://leadgreen.ai/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/katonic-dev/leadgreen-ai"
license: CC-BY-4.0
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23478909"
authors:
  - family-names: "Naraindas"
    given-names: "Prem"
    affiliation: Katonic
  - name: "Katonic AI Technology Ltd (Lead Green, a Katonic project)"
abstract: "Lead Green is a public index of LLM inference energy per token: the GPU energy it takes to serve a million output tokens (watt-hours per million output tokens), by model, GPU and configuration, with grid carbon intensity to price it anywhere, published as open data with a JSON API and an MCP server under CC BY 4.0. Every figure comes from a named public source with a retrieval date; it is a Katonic project, run and paid for by Katonic, and takes no money from hardware, cloud or model vendors. GPU energy only, measured at steady state on a busy server (the most energy-efficient configuration under a latency limit). Host, network, cooling and idle time are not counted. Every figure is a floor; a lightly used server sits well above it."
keywords:
  - "LLM inference energy"
  - "watt-hours per token"
  - "GPU energy"
  - "grid carbon intensity"
  - "green AI"
  - "open data"
  - "MCP server"
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    title: "The ML.ENERGY Benchmark: Toward Automated Inference Energy Measurement and Optimization"
    authors:
      - name: Chung et al.
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.06371"
    notes: NeurIPS 2025 Datasets and Benchmarks
